  "notes": "Night sky; only two paths for «يسارعون في الإثم» (the fork carries the warning); nothing illustrates the blamed acts. Their «آمنا» is glossed as «نفاقا ومكرا». STAGING v4: A market at dusk. 61: three men come to the believers (61:2) and speak (61:3, their outward claim); they walk back on 61:10 (they left as they came, Al-Muyassar: their entering and leaving are with disbelief). 62: the believers have left; one man in fine robes (standing for the rabbis and scholars) stands silent at one side while the three (only part of them: many of them) hasten to the centre on 62:4 and talk on 62:6 (lying words, Al-Muyassar); two paths then coins plates for sin and the unlawful gain. 63: the camera holds on the silent rabbis on 63:3 and 63:10 (their failure to forbid); nobody is shown forbidding."
